## Why This Is Asked

This question probes a beginner-friendly yet realistic E2E scenario: draft persistence, UI interactions, and end-to-end verification across multiple pages (feed and profile), with API mocking and test data isolation.

## Key Concepts

- LocalStorage persistence and autosave behavior
- End-to-end API mocking with intercept/stub
- Test data seeding and isolation
- Cross-page assertions and state verification

## Code Example

```javascript
// Cypress example
describe('Drafts and Publish', () => {
  beforeEach(() => {
    // Seed test user
    cy.request('POST', '/api/test/setup', { user: 'test-user' }).then(() => {
      // Mock the publish API
      cy.intercept('POST', '/api/posts', {
        statusCode: 201,
        body: { id: '123', status: 'published' }
      }).as('publishPost');
    });
    cy.visit('/compose');
  });

  it('autosaves draft, preserves on reload, and publishes to feed and profile', () => {
    // Compose a draft
    cy.get('.rich-text-editor').type('My new post draft');

    // Wait for autosave (15 seconds)
    cy.wait(15000);
    cy.window().then(win => {
      expect(win.localStorage.getItem('draft')).to.exist;
    });

    // Reload and verify draft restoration
    cy.reload();
    cy.get('.rich-text-editor').should('contain', 'My new post draft');

    // Publish the post
    cy.get('[data-testid="publish-btn"]').click();
    cy.wait('@publishPost');

    // Verify draft is cleared
    cy.window().then(win => {
      expect(win.localStorage.getItem('draft')).to.be.null;
    });

    // Verify post appears in main feed
    cy.visit('/feed');
    cy.contains('My new post draft').should('be.visible');

    // Verify post appears on profile
    cy.visit('/profile/test-user');
    cy.contains('My new post draft').should('be.visible');
  });
});
```

## Tool Selection

**Cypress** is recommended for beginners due to its intuitive API, excellent debugging tools, and automatic waiting for elements and commands.

## Test Isolation

Each test runs in a fresh browser context with a clean localStorage state, ensuring no data leaks between tests.

## Purpose

This question evaluates practical E2E testing skills, specifically around runtime feature flags, test data seeding, and UI assertions in a social application context.

## Key Concepts

- Feature flag rollout strategies
- Test data seeding for user cohorts
- Mocking remote config services
- UI assertions for different feature states
- Stability under mid-flight config changes

## Code Example

```javascript
const { test, expect } = require('@playwright/test');

test('feature-flag gated composer', async ({ page, context }) => {
  // Seed users and mock remote config
  const userA = await seedUser({ cohort: 0 });
  const userB = await seedUser({ cohort: 1 });

  await context.addCookies([
    { name: 'user_id', value: userA.id, domain: 'localhost' },
    { name: 'cohort', value: '0', domain: 'localhost' }
  ]);

  // Mock remote config for 10% rollout to cohort 1
  await page.route('**/remote-config', async (route) => {
    route.fulfill({ json: { composer_rollout: { cohort: 1, percentage: 10 } } });
  });

  // Verify cohort 0 sees old composer
  await page.goto('/home');
  await expect(page.locator('.old-composer')).toBeVisible();
  await expect(page.locator('.new-composer')).not.toBeVisible();

  // Post and verify
  await page.fill('.tweet-input', 'Tweet from cohort 0');
  await page.click('.submit-tweet');
  await expect(page.locator('.tweet:has-text("Tweet from cohort 0")')).toBeVisible();
});

test('mid-session config flip', async ({ page }) => {
  await page.addInitScript(() => {
    window.__INITIAL_CONFIG__ = { composer_rollout: { cohort: 1, percentage: 0 } };
  });

  await page.goto('/home');
  await expect(page.locator('.old-composer')).toBeVisible();

  // Flip config mid-session
  await page.addInitScript(() => {
    window.__REMOTE_CONFIG__ = { composer_rollout: { cohort: 1, percentage: 100 } };
  });
  await page.reload();

  await expect(page.locator('.new-composer')).toBeVisible();
});
```

## What Good Answers Demonstrate

- Understanding of Playwright fundamentals (page objects, context, routing)
- Knowledge of feature flag architecture and cohort-based rollouts
- Ability to mock external services for deterministic testing
- Consideration of edge cases like mid-flight config changes
- Clean, maintainable test structure with clear assertions

